    "https://cuny.jobs/258115232D844523B22346DBE530C2A425": {
      "title": "Anatomist - Med Faculty Open Rank",
      "description": "Anatomist - Med Faculty Open Rank. Anatomist - Med Faculty Open Rank **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The CUNY School of Medicine (CUNY SoM) located in the heart of Harlem, New York, is the only medical school in the City University of New York system and the only public medical school in Manhattan. Building upon 50 years of success as the Sophie Davis School of Biomedical Education, the institution transitioned to the CUNY School of Medicine (SoM) in 2016. The CUNY SoM offers an accelerated BS/MD degree (7-year program), Post-baccalaureate Masters program (1-year), and a Physician Assistant Master's Degree (27 months program). True to its legacy of access, opportunity, and community transformation, the medical school's mission remains to recruit highly talented students as diverse as New York City itself. CUNY SoM places a special emphasis on the recruitment of those who are underrepresented in the field of medicine and on training high quality, supremely competent health professionals and scientists equipped to address the healthcare needs of New York's medically under-served communities. As a major priority, CUNY SoM also seeks to enhance the recruitment and retention of senior leadership, faculty, and staff to more closely reflect our student body. The CUNY SoM has five departments: Department of Molecular, Cellular, and Biomedical Sciences (MCBS) was formed through the merger of several basic science departments and represents one of the four departments in the school (Community Health and Social Medicine, Medical Education, and Clinical Medicine). All departments plays a critical role in our mission-driven BS/MD program, post-bac program and Physician Assistant program through the teaching of the basic science curriculum and by conducting extramurally funded research. The research agenda of the current members of the departments are centered on neuroscience, microbiology and immunology, cardiovascular disease, oncology, social determinants of health, and community health. The selected candidate will be placed in the most appropriate department based upon their credentials and experience. Reporting to the Chair of either the MCBS, Medical Education, CHASM or Clinical Medicine department, the Anatomist will be responsible for but not limited to the following: + Postdoctoral or fellowship training or equivalent advanced research experience in Anatomy or related biomedical or clinical sciences. + Teach gross human anatomy to medical and PA students in lecture, laboratory, and small group settings, including cadaveric dissection + Serve as a content expert in anatomy and contribute to integrated, systems-based, and clinically relevant curricula + Contribute to instruction in embryology and histology as needed within organ-system-based or other integrated curricular frameworks + Develop, implement, and evaluate anatomy curriculum components, including laboratory-based and technology-enhanced learning (e.g., simulation, digital anatomy platforms, 3D imaging) + Lead student-centered learning sessions across lecture, prosection, small group, and laboratory formats + Participate in assessment activities, including laboratory practical examinations, OSCEs, and curriculum evaluation + Collaborate with faculty across disciplines to align instruction with institutional Educational Program Objectives (EPOs), foundational competencies, and course-level learning outcomes + Mentor and advise students in academic success and scholarly development + Serve on institutional committees, including curriculum and admissions committees + Engage in scholarly activity + Uphold an inclusive and equitable learning environment consistent with CUNY SOMs mission + Perform other duties as assigned by the Chair of the Department **QUALIFICATIONS** + Doctoral degree (Ph.D., D.O., M.D., or equivalent) in anatomy, or a related health sciences field + Demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence and student-centered learning in classroom, laboratory, or related instructional settings, including cadaveric or prosection-based anatomy **PREFERRED:** + Postdoctoral or fellowship training or equivalent advanced research experience in Anatomy or related biomedical or clinical sciences + Experience teaching gross human anatomy in a medical, PA, or other health professions program + Experience teaching embryology, histology, or neuroanatomy within organ-system-based or integrated health professions curricula + Experience with prosection- and dissection-based laboratory instruction, including cadaveric laboratory management + Experience collaborating across pre-clerkship and clinical phases of MD training + Proficiency with active learning methodologies, including PBL, CBL, and TBL + Background in curriculum development, course administration, and assessment design, including laboratory practical examinations and course improvement initiatives + Experience with educational technologies such as digital anatomy platforms, simulation, virtual reality, or other digital learning tools + Experience teaching clinically relevant medical imaging (ultrasound, radiography, CT, MRI, 3D imaging) in support of anatomy instruction + Experience with student coaching, feedback, and practical or OSCE-related assessment + Evidence of scholarly activity through publications, presentations, educational research, or grant-supported work in anatomy, medical education, or a related field + Familiarity with FERPA, HIPAA, and relevant academic, clinical, and laboratory compliance requirements **COMPENSATION** **Medical Faculty (Open Rank)** _Tenure-Track Appointments_ + Medical Assistant Professor (Basic Science): $80,982 $128,748 + Medical Associate Professor (Basic Science): $100,052 $149,375 + Medical Professor (Basic Science): $119,128 $169,995 _NonTenure-Track Appointments_ + Medical Clinical Professor (Med Series): $79,127 $227,755 Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates should provide a CV/resume and statement of scholarly interests. **CLOSING DATE** Open until filled. Review of resumes to begin on July 1, 2026. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32385 Location: CUNY School of Medicine"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/B7A9ACBFFF53400594927F550AEECC8025": {
      "title": "Pharmacologist - Med Faculty Open Rank",
      "description": "Pharmacologist - Med Faculty Open Rank. Pharmacologist - Med Faculty Open Rank **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The CUNY School of Medicine (CUNY SoM) located in the heart of Harlem, New York, is the only medical school in the City University of New York system and the only public medical school in Manhattan. Building upon 50 years of success as the Sophie Davis School of Biomedical Education, the institution transitioned to the CUNY School of Medicine (SoM) in 2016. The CUNY SoM offers an accelerated BS/MD degree (7-year program), Post-baccalaureate Masters program (1-year), and a Physician Assistant Master's Degree (27 months program). True to its legacy of access, opportunity, and community transformation, the medical school's mission remains to recruit highly talented students as diverse as New York City itself. CUNY SoM places a special emphasis on the recruitment of those who are underrepresented in the field of medicine and on training high quality, supremely competent health professionals and scientists equipped to address the healthcare needs of New York's medically under-served communities. As a major priority, CUNY SoM also seeks to enhance the recruitment and retention of senior leadership, faculty, and staff to more closely reflect our student body. The CUNY SoM has five departments: Department of Molecular, Cellular, and Biomedical Sciences (MCBS) was formed through the merger of several basic science departments and represents one of the four departments in the school (Community Health and Social Medicine, Medical Education, and Clinical Medicine). All departments play a critical role in our mission-driven BS/MD program, post-bac program and Physician Assistant program through the teaching of the basic science curriculum and by conducting extramurally funded research. The research agenda of the current members of the departments are centered on neuroscience, microbiology and immunology, cardiovascular disease, oncology, social determinants of health, and community health. The selected candidate will be placed in the most appropriate department based upon their credentials and experience. Reporting to the Chair of either the MCBS, Medical Education, CHASM or Clinical Medicine department, duties include but at not limited to: + Provide leadership in the planning, delivery, and evaluation of undergraduate, graduate, and postgraduate medical education programs. + Deliver high-quality classroom, clinical, laboratory, and bedside teaching to medical students, PA students and other healthcare trainees. + Develop, review, and enhance curricula, educational resources, and assessment strategies to ensure alignment with accreditation standards and advances in medical practice. + Assess learner performance through examinations, clinical evaluations, competency-based assessments, and other educational activities. + Supervise and mentor medical students, PA students, and other train academic, clinical, and professional development. + Maintain an active program of scholarly activity through educational research, clinical research, publications, presentations, and other academic contributions. + Participate in and lead interdisciplinary clinical, educational, and research initiatives that promote excellence in patient care and medical education. + Contribute to quality improvement, patient safety, evidence-based practice, and innovation in clinical and educational settings. + Provide academic and administrative leadership in program development, accreditation activities, faculty development, and strategic planning initiatives. + Serve on departmental, institutional, and university committees, contributing to governance, policy development, community engagement, and institutional advancement. + Perform other duties as assigned by the Chair of the Department **QUALIFICATIONS** + Doctoral degree (Ph.D., D.O., M.D., or equivalent). + Demonstrated knowledge of pharmacology. **PREFERRED:** + Experience in teaching, training, or mentoring, preferably in a higher education setting. + Excellent communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills. + Ability to engage, motivate, and support student learning. + Commitment to continuous professional development and lifelong learning. + Previous teaching experience in a higher education institution. + Experience with curriculum development and instructional design. + Record of scholarly research and publications. + Membership in relevant professional organizations. + Experience contributing to academic program development and assessment. **COMPENSATION** **Medical Faculty (Open Rank)** _Tenure-Track Appointments_ + Medical Assistant Professor (Basic Science): $80,982 $128,748 + Medical Associate Professor (Basic Science): $100,052 $149,375 + Medical Professor (Basic Science): $119,128 $169,995 _NonTenure-Track Appointments_ + Medical Clinical Professor (Med Series): $79,127 $227,755 Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates should provide a CV/resume and statement of scholarly interests. **CLOSING DATE** Open until filled. Review of resumes to begin on July 28, 2026. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32492 Location: CUNY School of Medicine"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/BF9F347712CC48769963125FD495416325": {
      "title": "Artificial Intelligence/ Biomedical Analytics - Med Asst Professor Basic",
      "description": "Artificial Intelligence/ Biomedical Analytics - Med Asst Professor Basic. Artificial Intelligence/ Biomedical Analytics - Med Asst Professor Basic **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The City University of New York (CUNY) School of Medicine (SoM) is the only medical school in the CUNY system. Our innovative curriculum allows students to complete both their undergraduate Bachelor of Science (BS) and Doctor of Medicine (MD) degrees in seven years. CUNY SoM graduated its first MD class in 2020. In addition, the CUNY SoM offers a two-year Physician Assistant (PA) program to prepare health professionals licensed to practice medicine with physician supervision. Our mission is 1) to provide access to medical education to talented youth from historically underrepresented in backgrounds in medicine and to develop health professionals committed to practicing in under-served communities and 2) to perform innovative research in community health and biomedicine. The Department of Molecular, Cellular & Biomedical Sciences (MCBS) is a dynamic center of research and innovation, with faculty members leading active, NIH-funded programs in cutting-edge areas, including neuroscience, cardiovascular sciences, and drug discovery. Faculty in the department mentor doctoral students through CUNY Graduate Center programs in neuroscience, cognitive neuroscience, molecular and developmental biology, chemistry, and biochemistry. The MCBS Department at the CUNY School of Medicine invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Medical Professor (Basic Science). Reporting to the Chair of the MCBS department, duties include but are not limited to: + Develop and maintain an independent, externally funded research program in artificial intelligence (AI), bioinformatics, genomics, computational biology, biostatistics, or a related field. + Conduct innovative research using large-scale biomedical datasets, including electronic health records (EHR), genomic data, medical imaging, and clinical trial data, to advance translational research and improve health outcomes. + Collaborate with faculty across the Departments of Molecular, Cellular & Biomedical Sciences, Community Health and Social Medicine, Clinical Medicine, and the Center for Advancing Translational Research and Health (CART), as well as with external academic, clinical, and community partners. + Develop computational methods, statistical models, and AI-driven approaches to address challenges in healthcare, medical diagnostics, healthcare access and utilization, and precision medicine, with an emphasis on reducing health disparities. + Secure extramural research funding from federal agencies, foundations, and other sponsors. + Teach and mentor medical students, graduate students, and trainees in areas related to AI, bioinformatics, data science, and biomedical research. + Contribute to the development of educational and training initiatives that strengthen AI and bioinformatics competencies among researchers, physicians, and other healthcare professionals. + Publish scholarly research in peer-reviewed journals and present findings at national and international scientific meetings. + Participate in departmental, school, and university service, including committee work, curriculum development, and other faculty responsibilities. + Perform other duties as assigned by the Chair of the Department **QUALIFICATIONS** + Doctoral degree (Ph.D. or., M.D.,). in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Bioinformatics, Biostatistics, Data Science, or a closely related field from an accredited institution + 3-5 years of postdoctoral research experience and an emerging record of scientific publications **PREFERRED:** + Experience with cloud computing platforms and related technologies. + Demonstrated application of artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning (ML), or advanced analytical techniques to medical imaging, genomics, electronic health records (EHR), and other clinical or preclinical datasets. + Familiarity with healthcare data formats and standards, including DICOM, HL7, and other clinical data protocols. + Record of publications in AI/ML, biomedical informatics, healthcare analytics, or related journals and conferences. + Prior experience working in multidisciplinary academic or medical research environments. + Experience with experimental design, grant proposal development, and scientific manuscript preparation. **COMPENSATION** Salary Range: $80,982 $128,748 Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates should provide a CV/resume and statement of scholarly interests. **CLOSING DATE** Open until filled. Review of resumes to begin on July 30, 2026. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32510 Location: CUNY School of Medicine"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/8B45F500610B49EBA2F1777EF7B9CDC125": {
      "title": "Didactic/Clinical Coordinator (Med Dist Lecturer) - Physician Assistant Program",
      "description": "Didactic/Clinical Coordinator (Med Dist Lecturer) - Physician Assistant Program. Didactic/Clinical Coordinator (Med Dist Lecturer) - Physician Assistant Program **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The CUNY School of Medicine (CUNY SoM) located in the heart of Harlem, New York, is the only medical school in the City University of New York system and the only public medical school in Manhattan. Building upon 50 years of success as the Sophie Davis School of Biomedical Education, the institution transitioned to the CUNY School of Medicine (SoM) in 2016. The CUNY SoM offers an accelerated BS/MD degree (7-year program) and a Physician Assistant Masters Degree (28-month program). True to its legacy of access, opportunity, and community transformation, the medical schools mission remains to recruit highly talented students as diverse as New York City itself. CUNY SoM places a special emphasis on the recruitment of those who are underrepresented in the field of medicine and on training high quality, culturally competent health professionals and scientists equipped to address the healthcare needs of New Yorks medically under-served communities. As a major priority, CUNY SoM also seeks to enhance the recruitment and retention of senior leadership, faculty, and staff to more closely reflect the diversity of our student body. Under the direction of the Associate Dean/Program Director, the Didactic/Clinical Coordinator for the Physician Assistant (PA) Program will provide instruction in areas of expertise and perform related clinical, faculty, and administrative duties. The Didactic/Clinical Coordinator will be an experienced practitioner and educator who holds a full-time position subject to annual reappointment. The individual will share responsibility for committee, program, and departmental assignments, including administrative, supervisory, and other related functions. Additional responsibilities of the Didactic/Clinical Coordinator include, but are not limited to, the following: + Maintain ongoing program and student evaluation processes to ensure the quality and effectiveness of instruction within the PA Program; develop and revise learning objectives for courses as appropriate. + Review and revise student handbooks and program policies annually and ensure students meet all required certifications, immunizations, and other requirements necessary for participation in clinical clerkships. + Evaluate students and instructors; develop student assessment instruments consistent with course objectives; and monitor individual student progress throughout the didactic year. + Develop examinations, assessment tools, and test-item analyses to evaluate student learning and program effectiveness. + Participate in program activities, including student admissions, curriculum development, and student evaluation. + Participate in activities necessary to support the maintenance of program accreditation. + Serve as a faculty advisor to professional students. + Serve as a liaison between the PA Program and preceptors at established clinical sites; identify and secure clinical sites consistent with program objectives; and maintain an ongoing site evaluation process to ensure the quality of clinical instruction. + Provide direction and oversight for student clinical rotations at assigned clinical sites; develop and revise learning objectives for each rotation; review and update the Clinical and Preceptor Handbooks annually; and co-coordinate the annual Clinical Year Orientation. + Identify and secure qualified adjunct faculty instructors consistent with the objectives and instructional needs of the PA Program. + Perform other related duties as assigned by the Associate Dean/Program Director. **QUALIFICATIONS** + Master of Science degree from an accredited Physician Assistant (PA) Program. + Minimum of five years of clinical experience and experience in Physician Assistant education. + Current National Commission on Certification of Physician Assistants (NCCPA) board certification. + Current New York State Physician Assistant license. **PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS** + PA-C, Master's degree or doctorate degree with 5 years of experience in Physician Assistant education. + Experience providing hospital-based inpatient Physician Assistant clinical care and working within associated subspecialties. + Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Outlook, Word, Access, and Excel. + Strong organizational, interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills. + Detail-oriented and accurate, with strong quantitative, scientific, clinical, and critical-thinking skills. + Demonstrated commitment to diversity and to fostering an inclusive academic environment that supports various forms of inquiry and scholarship across multiple disciplines. + Thorough understanding of the importance of diversity in academic medicine, including experience working in an urban setting and an understanding of disparities within academic medicine. + Demonstrated leadership skills and the ability to promote cooperative and collaborative clinical initiatives with other college and CUNY units, as well as academic, clinical, educational, and industry partners. **COMPENSATION** Salary Range: $130,000 - $150,000 Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates should provide a CV/resume and statement of scholarly interests. **CLOSING DATE** Open until filled. Review of resumes to begin on September 5, 2026. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32672 Location: CUNY School of Medicine"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/2D4E88F29C6A4D46A2A42BB3263AA9C825": {
      "title": "Research Data Librarian (Medical Asst Professor)",
      "description": "Research Data Librarian (Medical Asst Professor). Research Data Librarian (Medical Asst Professor) **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The City University of New York (CUNY) School of Medicine (SoM) is the only medical school in the CUNY system. Our innovative curriculum allows students to complete both their undergraduate Bachelor of Science (BS) and Doctor of Medicine (MD) degrees in seven years. CUNY SoM graduated its first MD class in 2020. In addition, the CUNY SoM offers a two-year Physician Assistant (PA) program to prepare health professionals licensed to practice medicine with physician supervision. Our mission is 1) to provide access to medical education to talented youth from historically underrepresented in backgrounds in medicine and to develop health professionals committed to practicing in under-served communities and 2) to perform innovative research in community health and biomedicine. The School of Medicine is currently seeking a Research Data Librarian. Reporting to the Chief Librarian, this position provides expertise and support for research data management, data-related scholarly communications, and evidence synthesis activities at the CUNY Medicine. This position serves as a key member of the library's research support team, partnering with faculty, researchers, staff, and students throughout the research lifecycle. The librarian assists researchers in developing data management and sharing plans, promotes best practices for research data stewardship, and supports compliance with funder and institutional requirements. In addition, the position provides library instruction, reference services, and collaborates with research teams on systematic and scoping reviews. The Research Data Librarian duties include but are not limited to the following responsibilities: + Consult with faculty, researchers, staff, and students on research data management best practices throughout the research lifecycle; assist researchers in developing data management and sharing plans for grant proposals and sponsored research projects. + Advise researchers on data organization, documentation, metadata standards, storage, preservation, sharing, and reuse; provide guidance regarding compliance with federal, institutional, and publisher requirements related to data management and data sharing. + Develop instructional materials, workshops, and online resources related to research data management and data literacy; collaborate with institutional stakeholders to promote responsible data stewardship and open science practices. + Monitor emerging trends, technologies, policies, and standards related to research data services. + Administer and maintain researcher profile platform (Pure or another similar system); configure system settings, workflows, integrations, and user permissions; monitor platform performance and coordinate upgrades, testing, and troubleshooting. + Collaborate with IT staff, vendors, and system administrators to ensure system reliability; manage researcher profile data, including publications, grants, patents, awards, etc.; perform data cleanup, deduplication, validation, and authority control. + Integrate data from databases and research identification systems such as ORCID, Crossref, and Scopus. + Partner with faculty, clinicians, researchers, and students on systematic reviews, scoping reviews, and other evidence synthesis projects; design, execute, and document comprehensive literature search strategies across biomedical databases; contribute to review methodology, search reproducibility, citation management, and reporting standards. + Serve as a co-author on systematic reviews and other scholarly publications when contributions meet accepted authorship criteria; provide bibliographic instruction, reference and research consultation services; create guides, tutorials, and instructional materials supporting evidence-based practice and information literacy. + Participate in library planning, assessment, committees, and strategic initiatives; engage in professional development and scholarship; contribute to the profession through presentations, publications, and service activities. + Perform other duties as assigned by the Chief Librarian or designee **QUALIFICATIONS** **MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS** + Masters degree in Library Science, Masters in Library and Information Studies, or closely related discipline from an ALA-accredited institution; a second graduate degree is required. + Experience conducting advanced literature searches in biomedical and health sciences databases. + Knowledge of research data management principles and practices. + Demonstrated ability to provide instruction and consultation services. + Strong organizational, analytical, and communication skills. + Ability to work collaboratively with diverse stakeholders in a research-intensive environment. **PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS** + Experience supporting grant-funded research and developing data management and sharing plans. + Experience participating in systematic reviews, scoping reviews, or other evidence synthesis projects. + Familiarity with NIH Data Management and Sharing Policy and other federal funding agency requirements. + Knowledge of data repositories, metadata standards, and data sharing practices. + Experience with implementation of the Elsevier Pure product or a similar researcher profile system. + Experience with citation management software and evidence synthesis tools. + Experience in academic health sciences or medical libraries. + Record of scholarly activity, including presentations, publications, or professional service. **COMPENSATION** Medical Assistant Professor (Basic Science): $80,982 $128,748 Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates should provide a CV/resume and statement of scholarly interests. **CLOSING DATE** Open until filled. Review of resumes to begin on August 27, 2026. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32634 Location: CUNY School of Medicine"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/D0567D794B67491D83A0BC434E80F59E25": {
      "title": "Family Medicine Clerkship Director (Med Clinical Prof-Med Series)",
      "description": "Family Medicine Clerkship Director (Med Clinical Prof-Med Series). Family Medicine Clerkship Director (Med Clinical Prof-Med Series) **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The City University of New York (CUNY) School of Medicine (SoM) is the only medical school in the CUNY system. Our innovative curriculum allows students to complete both their undergraduate Bachelor of Science (BS) and Doctor of Medicine (MD) degrees in seven years. CUNY SoM graduated its first MD class in 2020. In addition, the CUNY SoM offers a two-year Physician Assistant (PA) program to prepare health professionals licensed to practice medicine with physician supervision. Our mission is 1) to provide access to medical education to talented youth from historically underrepresented in backgrounds in medicine and to develop health professionals committed to practicing in under-served communities and 2) to perform innovative research in community health and biomedicine. As a community-based medical school, CUNY SOM delivers clinical education through partnerships with affiliated health institutions across the New York metropolitan area. Based at the Harlem campus, the Family Medicine Clerkship Director oversees clerkship implementation, serving as a liaison among students, faculty, and school administration. The Clerkship Director also collaborates with site directors and affiliate faculty to organize and implement teaching and assessment across all clinical sites. The successful candidate will be appointed as a Clinical Professor Medical Series, a full-time, non-tenure-track position in the Department of Clinical Medicine, reporting to the Department Chair. The Clerkship Director will join a team of mission-driven educators and scholars and will have access to collaborative and mentorship opportunities across departments, including Medical Education, Community Health and Social Medicine (CHASM), Library Sciences, and Molecular, Cellular and Biomedical Sciences (MCBS). Opportunities are also available to leverage the institutions research infrastructure in support of scholarly interests. Duties include, but are not limited to: + Develop, implement, and evaluate a standardized didactic curriculum in Family Medicine for third-year medical students across all clinical sites. + Lead interactive, student-centered educational sessions (typically one afternoon per week). + Direct the simulation-based end-of-clerkship OSCE at the NYSIM Center at NYC Health + Hospitals/Bellevue. + Ensure alignment of teaching with national curricular guidelines, CUNY SOM Educational Program Objectives (EPOs), Foundational Competencies (FCs), and clerkship-level learning objectives. + Chair Clerkship Grading Committee meetings, oversee grading processes, and provide feedback to clinical site directors on evaluation practices. + Conduct periodic clinical site visits to ensure consistency in student experiences and assessment practices. + Oversee advanced clinical rotations, including fourth-year Family Medicine electives and sub-internships. + Participate in institutional committees (e.g., Curriculum Committee, Admissions Committee). + Mentor students and serve as a faculty advisor for student organizations, including the Family Medicine Special Interest Group (SIG). + Contribute to broader medical education efforts, including teaching in courses such as Practice of Medicine (POM), Organ Systems, Anatomy, Clinical Skills Assessment, and Introduction to Internship (ITI), as well as being the course director for an annual one week course for M3/M4 medical students. + Perform other duties as assigned by the Chair of the Clinical Medicine department This full-time position includes dedicated time for clinical practice, with flexible scheduling to accommodate clinical responsibilities. The institution provides support for professional development, including participation in regional and national medical education conferences. **QUALIFICATIONS** **MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:** + Medical degree from an accredited university. + Must be a board-certified Family Medicine physician. + Licensed or license-eligible in New York State. + Minimum of five years of experience as a Clerkship Director or in educational leadership, teaching medical students and/or residents. + Skilled educator with the ability to perform bedside and classroom teaching. + Strong administrative skills. **PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:** + Experience in faculty, curriculum, and assessment development and in advising medical students. + Knowledge of and ability to utilize advising practices and principles that inclusively and equitably serve a diverse student population in a variety of settings. + Demonstrated record of professional achievement and a willingness to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students from a wide range of disciplines, cultures, and academic backgrounds for the good of the institution. + Demonstrated commitment to promoting diversity, inclusion, and multicultural and structural competence in a learning environment. **COMPENSATION** **Salary Range: $175,000 - $235,726** Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates should provide a CV/resume and statement of scholarly interests. **CLOSING DATE** Open until closed. Review of resumes to begin on October 15, 2026. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32880 Location: CUNY School of Medicine"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/D45FAB1785194778BFC6E4DE42E482F625": {
      "title": "Medical Student Advisor and Learning Community Facilitator (Med Clinical Prof-Med Series)",
      "description": "Medical Student Advisor and Learning Community Facilitator (Med Clinical Prof-Med Series). Medical Student Advisor and Learning Community Facilitator (Med Clinical Prof-Med Series) **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The City University of New York (CUNY) School of Medicine (SoM) is the only medical school in the CUNY system. Our innovative curriculum allows students to complete both their undergraduate Bachelor of Science (BS) and Doctor of Medicine (MD) degrees in seven years. CUNY SoM graduated its first MD class in 2020. In addition, the CUNY SoM offers a two-year Physician Assistant (PA) program to prepare health professionals licensed to practice medicine with physician supervision. Our mission is 1) to provide access to medical education to talented youth from historically underrepresented in backgrounds in medicine and to develop health professionals committed to practicing in under-served communities and 2) to perform innovative research in community health and biomedicine. CSOM is seeking a qualified candidate to serve as a Medical Student Advisor and Learning Community Facilitator in a non-tenure-track position under the contractual title of Medical Clinical ProfessorMed Series. Individuals appointed to the Medical Clinical ProfessorMed Series are experienced practitioners and educators in their respective fields. The Medical Student Advisor and Learning Community Facilitator will guide and support medical students throughout their education, including career planning, clinical rotations, board examinations (such as the USMLE), and residency matching. The successful candidate will also review students academic performance and work closely with faculty, course directors, and the Student Affairs Department to support student success and prepare students to become ethical medical practitioners and scientists. Reporting directly to the Associate Dean for Student Affairs, the Medical Student Advisor and Learning Community Facilitator will be responsible for but not limited to: + Advising medical students on career choice & residency planning and facilitate individual or group educational sessions to students about Careers in Medicine. + Develop and conduct informational seminars and workshops (such as using the AAMC Careers in Medicine Program) for students to support academic, professional and personal growth including career opportunities and residency choice. + Conduct learning assessments and implement evidence-based strategies to help students improve performance, including preparation for NBME assessments and USMLE Step 1 and Step 2 exams. + Provide structured academic performance intervention strategies; including early identification, proactive outreach, and support contributions to individualized remediation plans for students at academic risk. + Meet regularly with students in one-on-one advising sessions regarding, academic challenges, medical careers, residency choice, fourth year planning and preparing for life after medical school. + In conjunction with the Associate Dean for Student Affairs, will meet individually with students and prepare the MSPE for students entering the Residency Match Program during year 7. + Serve on various college, medical school and university committees to give input relevant to the role of Medical Student Advisor. + Perform other duties as assigned by the Associate Dean of Student Affairs or designee.*This position will require some evening and weekend hours. **QUALIFICATIONS** **MINIMUM:** + MD, PhD or EdD and 2-5 years of experience in teaching and advising medical students and/or residents from a wide range of cultures, and academic backgrounds. + Experience in teach advising groups in the medical school portion years 4-7 of the 7-year BS/MD continuum. + Demonstrated commitment to building and promoting equitable, diverse and inclusive academic environments and must be willing to contribute to the CSOMs diversity and inclusion goals. + Commitment to promoting diversity, inclusion, and multicultural and structural competence in a learning environment. + Excellent communication (verbal and written) and people skills as well as excellent presentation skills - diversity + Knowledge of and ability to utilize advising practices and principles that inclusively and equitably serve a diverse student population in a variety of settings. + Experience teaching in large and small group settings + Must have demonstrated satisfactory qualities of personality and character, a record of achievements in his/her profession or field of expertise, and a willingness to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students from a wide range of disciplines, cultures, and academic backgrounds for the good of the institution. **PREFERRED:** + Knowledge of learning strategies, inclusive pedagogy, and experience coaching at risk students. + Knowledge of medical school and residency requirements regarding curriculum requirement, personal attributes and professional experiences (research, leadership, etc.). + Familiarity with MSPE letters and the ERAS match process for residency. + Familiarity with the LCME accreditation process. + Experience in managing a range of student affair issues. + Experience in supporting student academic success, particularly for members of underrepresented groups. **COMPENSATION** Salary Range: $150,000 - $175,000 Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates should provide a CV/resume and statement of scholarly interests. **CLOSING DATE** Open until closed. Review of resumes to begin on October 29, 2026. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32975 Location: CUNY School of Medicine"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/66919CBDE88F4F6B90DEEF420BEDE98C25": {
      "title": "Biostatistician - Med Faculty Open Rank",
      "description": "Biostatistician - Med Faculty Open Rank. Biostatistician - Med Faculty Open Rank **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The CUNY School of Medicine (CUNY MED) is the only medical school in the City University of New York system. Our innovative curriculum allows students to complete both their undergraduate Bachelor of Science (BS) and Doctor of Medicine (MD) degrees in seven years. CUNY MED graduated its first MD class in 2020. In addition, the CUNY MED offers a two-year Physician Assistant (PA) program to prepare health professionals licensed to practice medicine with physician supervision. Our mission is 1) to provide access to medical education to talented youth from historically underrepresented in backgrounds in medicine and to develop health professionals committed to practicing in under-served communities and 2) to perform innovative research in community health and biomedicine. The Department of Community Health and Social Medicine (CHASM) plays a central role in CUNY MEDs mission-driven BS/MD and Physician Assistant programs through its integrated teaching and research initiatives. The departments curricular responsibilities focus on educating students in the social, economic, political, and behavioral determinants of health and disease, with particular emphasis on population health, health disparities, and health care policy. CHASMs research portfolio includes chronic disease epidemiology, health behavior, health policy, health services research, and community-based participatory research. The Biostatistic faculty member will be either an Assistant, Associate or Full Professor who will play a pivotal role in enhancing the School of Medicine's biostatistical core, complement and deepen our current academic departments bioscience strengths. The Biostatistician will be the academic subject matter expert in Bayesian methods, big data, causal inference, clinical trials, machine learning, mobile health data, real world evidence, public health and medical intervention analysis. Reporting to the Department Chair of CHASM, the Biostatistician will be responsible for but not limited to the following: + Developing and leading an extramurally funded research programs in the theory, methods, and/or applications of statistics in health-related fields. + Initiating and maintaining collaborations with community health, population health and/or clinician scientists and enhance research projects using innovative designs and methods. + Teaching undergraduate and graduate level courses and advise master's and doctoral students in the biomedical sciences; Mentoring students, trainees, and junior faculty. + Developing and sustaining an extramurally funded research programs, collaborate with other health researchers, contribute to SoM teaching and research development mission. + Participate in multidisciplinary biomedical and computational collaborations with investigators across the SoM; Conduct methodological and applied research in biostatistics + Participate in departmental, institutional, and national activities and community organizations related to biostatistics and biomedical sciences. + Provide biostatistical support for the NIH funded Research Center for Minority Institution + Collaborate and provide biostatistical support for grant applications + Perform related duties as assigned by the Department Chairperson or designee **QUALIFICATIONS** M.D. or Ph.D. in Statistics, Biostatistics, or a closely related field, as well as a record of significant achievement in profession or field of expertise. **PREFERRED:** + Experience in developing and implementing novel statistical methods, experience collaborating with health scientists, and a passion for teaching and mentoring. + An extramurally funded research program in areas of particular interest to the School of Medicine, including computational science, population health, and Artificial Intelligence (AI). + Demonstrated experience in machine learning/Artificial intelligence and Bayesian methods. + Causal inference for observational, interventional studies, and clinical trials methodology experience. + Analytical skills of electronic health records and other real-world data is a plus. + A strong record of peer-reviewed publications and extramural funding commensurate with rank. + Demonstrated excellence in collaborative research in clinical and translational science. + Experience in biostatistics teaching and mentoring. + At the **Full Professor** level, evidence of sustained scholarly leadership and national or international recognition. + At the **Associate Professor** level, candidates are expected to have a strong track record of extramurally funded research in statistical methodology and its applications. + At the **Assistant Professor l** evel, candidates are expected to demonstrate a clearly defined area of research focus with a strong publication record. + Team player with exceptional communication skills and experience working in multicultural environments. + A deep understanding of the importance of health, education, and healthcare disparities in higher education, along with experience developing models to understand their impact on outcomes **COMPENSATION** **Med Faculty Basic - Open Rank** Medical Assistant Professor (Basic) - $80,982 - $128,748 Medical Associate Professor (Basic) - $100,052 - $149,375 Medical Professor (Basic) $119,128 - $169,995 Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates should provide a CV/resume and statement of scholarly interests. **CLOSING DATE** Open until filled. Review of resumes to begin on June 17, 2026. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32321 Location: CUNY School of Medicine"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/D602EA21BA2A4B92A3CA018582E43C6925": {
      "title": "Microbiologist - Med Faculty Open Rank",
      "description": "Microbiologist - Med Faculty Open Rank. Microbiologist - Med Faculty Open Rank **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The CUNY School of Medicine (CUNY SoM) located in the heart of Harlem, New York, is the only medical school in the City University of New York system and the only public medical school in Manhattan. Building upon 50 years of success as the Sophie Davis School of Biomedical Education, the institution transitioned to the CUNY School of Medicine (SoM) in 2016. The CUNY SoM offers an accelerated BS/MD degree (7-year program), Post-baccalaureate Masters program (1-year), and a Physician Assistant Master's Degree (27 months program). True to its legacy of access, opportunity, and community transformation, the medical school's mission remains to recruit highly talented students as diverse as New York City itself. CUNY SoM places a special emphasis on the recruitment of those who are underrepresented in the field of medicine and on training high quality, supremely competent health professionals and scientists equipped to address the healthcare needs of New York's medically under-served communities. As a major priority, CUNY SoM also seeks to enhance the recruitment and retention of senior leadership, faculty, and staff to more closely reflect t our student body. The CUNY SoM has five departments: Department of Molecular, Cellular, and Biomedical Sciences (MCBS) was formed through the merger of several basic science departments and represents one of the four departments in the school (Community Health and Social Medicine, Medical Education, and Clinical Medicine). All departments plays a critical role in our mission-driven BS/MD program, post-bac program and Physician Assistant program through the teaching of the basic science curriculum and by conducting extramurally funded research. The research agenda of the current members of the departments are centered on neuroscience, microbiology and immunology, cardiovascular disease, oncology, social determinants of health, and community health. The selected candidate will be placed in the most appropriate department based upon their credentials and experience. Reporting to the Chair of either the MCBS, Medical Education, CHASM or Clinical Medicine department, the Microbiologist will be responsible for but not limited to the following: + Teach medical microbiology within pre-clerkship and clinical courses for medical and PA students + Serve as a content expert contributing to integrated, systems-based curricula + Develop, implement, and evaluate microbiology components of the curriculum, including laboratory and technology-enhanced learning (simulation, digital platforms) + Lead student-centered learning sessions across lecture, small group, and laboratory formats + Participate in assessment activities, including curriculum evaluation + Collaborate with faculty across disciplines to align instruction with institutional educational program objectives (EPOs), foundational competencies, and course-level learning outcomes + Mentor and advise students on academic success and scholarly development + Serve on institutional committees, including curriculum and admissions + Engage in scholarly activity + Uphold an inclusive, equitable learning environment consistent with CUNY SOMs mission + Perform other duties as assigned by the Chair of the Department **QUALIFICATIONS** + Doctoral degree (Ph.D., D.O., M.D., or equivalent) in Microbiology, or a related health sciences field + Demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence and student-centered learning in classroom laboratory, or related instructional settings **PREFERRED:** + Postdoctoral or fellowship training or equivalent advanced research experience in microbiology or related biomedical or clinical sciences + Experience teaching medical microbiology in a medical, PA, or other health professions program + Familiarity with clinically integrated microbiology within organ-system-based curricula + Experience collaborating across pre-clerkship and clerkship phases of MD training + Proficiency with active learning methodologies, including PBL, CBL, and TBL + Background in curriculum development, course administration, and assessment design + Experience with educational technologies such as virtual microbiology platforms or other digital learning tools + Experience teaching clinically relevant laboratory and diagnostic methods (e.g., culture, microscopy and staining, molecular diagnostics, antimicrobial susceptibility testing) in support of microbiology instruction + Experience with student coaching and feedback + Evidence of scholarly activity through publications, presentations, educational research, or grant-supported work + Work within underserved populations + Demonstrated commitment to addressing educational, health, and healthcare disparities **COMPENSATION** **Medical Faculty (Open Rank)** _Tenure-Track Appointments_ + Medical Assistant Professor (Basic Science): $80,982 $128,748 + Medical Associate Professor (Basic Science): $100,052 $149,375 + Medical Professor (Basic Science): $119,128 $169,995 _NonTenure-Track Appointments_ + Medical Clinical Professor (Med Series): $79,127 $227,755 Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates should provide a CV/resume and statement of scholarly interests. **CLOSING DATE** Open until filled. Review of resumes to begin on July 1, 2026. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32388 Location: CUNY School of Medicine"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/357375F0ADDC42A78C27AF1CD1B8279925": {
      "title": "Pathologist - Med Faculty Open Rank",
      "description": "Pathologist - Med Faculty Open Rank. Pathologist - Med Faculty Open Rank **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The CUNY School of Medicine (CUNY SoM) located in the heart of Harlem, New York, is the only medical school in the City University of New York system and the only public medical school in Manhattan. Building upon 50 years of success as the Sophie Davis School of Biomedical Education, the institution transitioned to the CUNY School of Medicine (SoM) in 2016. The CUNY SoM offers an accelerated BS/MD degree (7-year program), Post-baccalaureate Masters program (1-year), and a Physician Assistant Master's Degree (27 months program). True to its legacy of access, opportunity, and community transformation, the medical school's mission remains to recruit highly talented students as diverse as New York City itself. CUNY SoM places a special emphasis on the recruitment of those who are underrepresented in the field of medicine and on training high quality, supremely competent health professionals and scientists equipped to address the healthcare needs of New York's medically under-served communities. As a major priority, CUNY SoM also seeks to enhance the recruitment and retention of senior leadership, faculty, and staff to more closely reflect t our student body. The CUNY SoM has five departments: Department of Molecular, Cellular, and Biomedical Sciences (MCBS) was formed through the merger of several basic science departments and represents one of the four departments in the school (Community Health and Social Medicine, Medical Education, and Clinical Medicine). All departments plays a critical role in our mission-driven BS/MD program, post-bac program and Physician Assistant program through the teaching of the basic science curriculum and by conducting extramurally funded research. The research agenda of the current members of the departments are centered on neuroscience, microbiology and immunology, cardiovascular disease, oncology, social determinants of health, and community health. The selected candidate will be placed in the most appropriate department based upon their credentials and experience. Reporting to the Chair of either the MCBS, Medical Education, CHASM or Clinical Medicine department, the Pathologist will be responsible for but not limited to the following: + Teach Pathology within pre-clerkship and clinical courses for medical and PA students + Serve as a content expert contributing to integrated, systems-based curricula + Develop, implement, and evaluate pathology components of the curriculum, including laboratory and technology-enhanced learning (digital platforms) + Lead student-centered learning sessions across lecture, small group, and laboratory formats + Participate in assessment activities, including practical examinations and curriculum evaluation + Collaborate with faculty across disciplines to align instruction with institutional educational program objectives (EPOs), foundational competencies, and course-level learning outcomes + Mentor and advise students on academic success and scholarly development + Serve on institutional committees, including the curriculum committee and admissions + Engage in scholarly activity + Uphold an inclusive, equitable learning environment consistent with CUNY SOMs mission + Perform other duties as assigned by the Chair of the Department + Collaborate with faculty members across disciplines to promote interdisciplinary teaching and research initiatives. + Engage in professional development activities, conferences, and scholarly communities to stay current in the field of pathology. + Perform other duties as assigned by the Chair of the Department **QUALIFICATIONS** + Doctoral degree (Ph.D., D.O., M.D., or equivalent) in Pathology or a closely related health sciences field + Demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence and student-centered learning in classroom laboratory, or related instructional settings **PREFERRED:** + Postdoctoral or fellowship training or equivalent advanced research experience in pathology or related biomedical or clinical sciences + Experience teaching pathology in a medical, PA, or other health professions program + Familiarity with clinically integrated pathology within organ-system-based curricula + Experience collaborating across pre-clerkship and clerkship phases of MD training + Proficiency with active learning methodologies, including PBL, CBL, and TBL + Background in curriculum development, course administration, and assessment design + Experience with educational technologies such as virtual pathology platforms, simulations or other digital learning tools + Experience with student coaching and feedback + Evidence of scholarly activity through publications, presentations, educational research, or grant-supported work + Work within underserved populations + Demonstrated commitment to addressing educational, health, and healthcare disparities **COMPENSATION** **Medical Faculty (Open Rank)** _Tenure-Track Appointments_ + Medical Assistant Professor (Basic Science): $80,982 $128,748 + Medical Associate Professor (Basic Science): $100,052 $149,375 + Medical Professor (Basic Science): $119,128 $169,995 _NonTenure-Track Appointments_ + Medical Clinical Professor (Med Series): $79,127 $227,755 Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates should provide a CV/resume and statement of scholarly interests. **CLOSING DATE** Open until filled. Review of resumes to begin on July 1, 2026. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32389 Location: CUNY School of Medicine"
    }
  },
